      "content": "14. NO SOONER…THAN / HARDLY…WHEN (INVERSION RULE)"
    },
    {
      "type": "comparisonTable",
      "headers": [
        "Conjunction Pair / Concept",
        "Core Distinction & SSC Application"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Until vs Unless",
          "'Until' is time-oriented (up to the point in time), whereas 'Unless' is condition-oriented (if not)."
        ],
        [
          "No sooner... than vs Hardly... when",
          "'No sooner' strictly pairs with 'than'; 'Hardly' or 'Scarcely' strictly pairs with 'when' or 'before'."
        ],
        [
          "So... that vs Such... that",
          "'So... that' modifies adjectives/adverbs, while 'Such... that' modifies noun phrases."
        ],
        [
          "Whether vs If",
          "'Whether' is used when offering choices/alternatives (often with 'or'); 'If' introduces conditional clauses."
        ]
      ],
      "id": "dm3gpjs"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "1fdnksy"
    },
